--Description:
-- Goal: list every distinct movie-ID (MID) in which Shah Rukh Khan appears.
-- Why TRIM(): sample data show leading blanks (e.g. ' nm0451321', ' Shah Rukh Khan');
--            trimming ensures the person-id join succeeds and the name filter matches.
-- Why pattern ‘%Shah%Khan%’: captures both “Shah Rukh Khan” and “Shahrukh Khan”.
-- Steps:
--   1. Join M_CAST to PERSON on cleaned PID.
--   2. Keep rows whose cleaned person name contains “Shah…Khan”.
--   3. Select distinct MID, limit 20 for inspection.
SELECT DISTINCT mc."MID"
FROM DB_IMDB.DB_IMDB."M_CAST"  mc
JOIN DB_IMDB.DB_IMDB."PERSON"  p
  ON TRIM(mc."PID") = TRIM(p."PID")
WHERE TRIM(p."Name") ILIKE '%Shah%Khan%'
LIMIT 20;
```
